title: "pallet-assets: migrate native-token deposits from Currency reserves to fungible holds"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `pallet-assets` no longer uses the deprecated `ReservableCurrency` trait for the native-token
      deposits it takes (asset-creation, asset-account, metadata and approval deposits). Those
      deposits are now taken as `fungible` holds under `HoldReason::Deposit`. Part of #12399 / #226.

      Config changes (breaking):
      - `type Currency` bound changes from `ReservableCurrency` to
        `fungible::{Inspect + MutateHold<Reason = RuntimeHoldReason>}`.
      - New `type RuntimeHoldReason: From<HoldReason<I>>` must be supplied (the runtime's aggregated
        `RuntimeHoldReason`). Runtimes must ensure their `pallet-balances` instance exposes
        `RuntimeHoldReason`.
      - New `type OldCurrency: Currency + ReservableCurrency`, retained only to drain pre-existing
        reserved deposits during the lazy migration; otherwise unused.

      Migration strategy (no mass iteration): the deposits are per-asset, per-account, per-metadata
      and per-approval, which is unbounded on Asset Hub, so there is no `OnRuntimeUpgrade`.
      Instead the migration is lazy:
      - New deposits are always taken as holds.
      - When a deposit is released (asset destroyed, account refunded, metadata/approval cleared,
        etc.) the pallet first releases from the new hold and unreserves any remainder from a
        pre-existing legacy reserve. Ownership transfer moves the held portion via
        `transfer_on_hold` and repatriates any legacy-reserved remainder.
      This drains old reserves over time as entities are torn down; nothing strands and no entry is
      iterated en masse.

      Note: `pallet-assets-holder` (which extends `pallet_assets::Config` and defines its own
      `RuntimeHoldReason` for *asset* holds) now disambiguates its references to
      `<T as Config>::RuntimeHoldReason`.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      Asset/account/metadata/approval deposits keep working unchanged. Existing reserved deposits
      are converted to holds lazily, as each deposit is returned or moved; no action is required and
      funds stay locked throughout.

crates:
  - name: pallet-assets
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-assets-holder
    bump: patch
